      },
      {
        "id": "8ddzCM6WgzjCOQc7",
        "title": "With your Group!",
        "content": {
          "type": "Question",
          "version": 1,
          "locked": false,
          "questionId": "S22tM0",
          "tiles": [
            {
              "id": "uWvfACzyuj2gan3u",
              "title": "What motion do you want to start with?",
              "fixedPosition": true,
              "content": {
                "type": "Text",
                "format": "html",
                "text": [
                  "<p>An important part of engineering is iteration: trying things and improving it over time. You can probably think of a LOT of different motions and functions that would be useful for your person. Over time, you will make prototypes with more features, but you probably won’t figure it out all at once.</p><p>One way to start is to focus on something very specific.</p><p>What is <u>one</u> motion or action that you think is especially important for this person? Why did you choose to start with that motion?</p>"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "wtd1jXFx6p5yTmNX",
              "title": "Write the name of the person you picked here!",
              "content": {
                "type": "Text",
                "format": "html",
                "text": [
                  "<p>You can try writing: [Person&#x27;s name] needs to be able to [make this motion]. This is a good motion to start with for them because _______________.</p>"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "yo1XgHt-d7GFMBl4",
        "title": "Pro Tip: Group Docs!",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>In this unit, sometimes you will make decisions in a pair or group. When you do that, you can record your decisions in a shared doc for your group.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
