      {
        "id": "D9bPbF4Y2HtaxBpz",
        "title": "Designs",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Here are a few designs for an initial prototype (the instructions are in handouts).</p><p>None of them is perfect. We added a few pros and cons for each one.</p><p>Decide which one your team will make, but also think about one improvement you can make to it that will be helpful for the person you chose.</p><p>It can be a big or small change, but it should be <em>feasible</em> - meaning, you should be able to actually make that improvement!</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "T1-7MGuIqH4j1ouh",
        "title": "A note on improvements",
        "display": "teacher",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>The students are likely to come up with different improvements than they initially designed. If you want, you can get them to start making the prototype and just describe their improvements at the end.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "mu5pf4EvJZkw-iPP",
        "title": "With your group!",
        "content": {
